# Branch Naming Convention

All branches must follow the `user/<github-login>/<description>` format.

## Get your exact GitHub username

```bash
if command -v gh &>/dev/null; then
  LOGIN=$(gh api user --jq .login 2>/dev/null)
else
  LOGIN=$(git config github.user 2>/dev/null)
fi
```

Never infer from git config `user.name` or email — the org username may differ (e.g. `jsmith-amd` not `jsmith`).

## Allowed branch prefixes

| Prefix | Created by |
|---|---|
| `user/<login>/<desc>` | Developers |
| `team/<name>/<desc>` | Teams |
| `bot/<bot>/<desc>` | CI automation |
| `collab/*` | Collaborative (new) |
| `collab-*` | Collaborative (legacy) |
| `revert-*` | GitHub auto-created |
| `copilot/*` | GitHub Copilot |
| `dependabot/*` | Dependabot |

## Description rules

- ASCII only — no Unicode, emoji, or special characters
- Hyphens, underscores, or dots as separators — no slashes
- No leading dot (e.g. `.fix-rdma` is invalid)
- Include a ticket ID if one exists: `user/<login>/JIRA-1234-fix-something`

## Create and push

```bash
DEFAULT=$(git remote show origin 2>/dev/null | awk '/HEAD branch/{print $NF}')
DEFAULT=${DEFAULT:-master}
git fetch origin
git checkout -b "user/${LOGIN}/short-description" origin/${DEFAULT}
git push -u origin "user/${LOGIN}/short-description"
```

See: https://amd.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EN/pages/1810205147/GitHub+Branch+Protection+Rulesets